cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CORAL in your research, please cite this software."
title: "CORAL: Coral reef Optimization for Adaptive Layouts"
type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Zondervan"
    given-names: "Edwin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-2659-1622"
    affiliation: "University of Twente"

version: "CORAL-R1"

repository-code: "https://github.com/zondervan-edwin_collab/CORAL"

license: "MIT"

abstract: >-
  CORAL (Coral reef Optimization for Adaptive Layouts) is a topology-aware
  optimization framework for chemical process superstructures. It combines
  coral-reef-inspired structural exploration with explicit topology repair
  and deterministic constrained nonlinear programming for continuous
  design-variable refinement. CORAL-R1 is the frozen reproducible research
  version associated with the initial process-superstructure study.

keywords:
  - process systems engineering
  - process optimization
  - superstructure optimization
  - topology optimization
  - nature-inspired optimization
  - coral reef optimization
  - nonlinear programming
  - chemical engineering
